Z||000007||88-DOHC||12-05-2001||11:11 PM||||I have seen all sorts of sub installs in Fiero's from mild to wild.  Personally I am going for wild (when I get to that point).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Anyway, if your not 6' or taller and don't have your seat all the way back, you can get simething to fit behind there speaker wise (it may not be Kicker, but thats ok, since there is stuff that is easily just as good, if not better).  The next question is how big a sub do you want? Will 8" be enough, 10", 12", etc...?  That really is the deciding factor in alot of cases as to what you buy and where you put it.  Personally I would look into JL Audio if 8" is what you want (JL 8W6-CR to be exact). If 10" is what you want but space is really a big issue, look into Illusion Audio then. They make speakers that have very shallow mounting depths. If you think one sub is enough (which it probably would be) and don't feel bad about sacrificing your passengers leg room, then put it behind there, or in the footwell like the above picture. Otherwise if you want something even bigger...well, you just moved into the "wild" category. Be prepared to fork over some bucks for custom work at that point.<p>[This message has been edited by 88-DOHC (edited 12-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||12-06-2001||01:12 AM||||Subs, That's almost a loaded question.<BR>Anyhow, If you do a search in the archives for "Fierosound" he has a decent setup. It requires cutting the first layer of the rear lower firewall. (It's double paneled) The cut out is used to sink in the magnet of the sub (or subs if you want 2).<BR>If you are tall and require the seat all the way back, you can do just one behind the passenger seat. Otherwise you can fit one behind each seat.<BR>His website is: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/</A> <P>Next is as shown above in the passenger footwell. There are many ways to do it. 8" and 10" are the best, a 12" will take up more space than what is shown above.<P>You can also do a search for AusFiero, He has a console that replaces the armrest/glovebox between the seats. His are set up for 8" or 10" single sub.<P>Next spot is the front trunk. Many make the box to fit up front. To get the sound inside some have made a duct that goes from the trunk to the floor . This requires the floor to be cut and a grate/cover over the hole. You can fit up to a 12".<P>Finally, Some have fit 6" and some 8" subs under the dash. If you look on the passenger side right where the foot pad is then look up, You can mount a small box there. This is also the spot where on 1986 thru 1988 Fiero's with Premium sound had the 5" subwoofer mounted. commonly refered to as the "stock sub location"<P>As for Kicker speakers, They make a very good speaker. Though you will need to watch depth's of the speakers and volume required (box size) to fit in certain locations.<P>The Fiero having a small interior can make it difficult to install a decent system. But with all the "creative" folks here, you should have no problem setting up your system. Just decide which setup appeals to you and go for it.<P>If you do a search on my name you'll see the system I installed. I use a Rockford Fosgate 8" in the passenger footwell and 4" component speakers in place of all the stock speakers. I'm running about 500W with surround sound in my car.<P>Good luck with whatever you decide.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
